Cra: a profile's history isn't expired after 90 days (GitHub #730). Chrome's
HistoryBackend deletes every visit older than kExpireDaysThreshold (90 days),
starting 30 s after the History database opens. Arc keeps a profile's whole
history (a user's Arc History: 301,818 visits back to June 2024) and its
command bar searches all of it; Cra's Chromium History lost 265,073 visits a
user had merged from Arc within a week. Deleting history on purpose (Clear
Browsing Data, the History page) doesn't go through the expirer and still works.

